# wgq install plan, run step by step by `qubes-ingest apply wgq`.
# Verbs are interpreted by the ingest script; nothing here is shell.
# Base template first: skipped automatically when already installed;
# otherwise qvm-template pulls the OFFICIAL debian-13-minimal, verified
# against ITL's keys -- the trust anchor everything here already rests on.
template debian-13-minimal
# Build the template: clones debian-13-minimal and bootstraps the salt
# connector over qvm-run. Slow the first time.
salt wgq.wg-template
# The same state applied INSIDE the template: packages and files.
salt-target debian-13-wgq wgq.wg-template
# Identity: creates the wgq custom labels (red edge / green filter /
# yellow mgmt / black template, named so the icons scope to wgq alone)
# and installs the icon files into dom0's /usr/share/icons. wg-mgmt,
# every zone and the template include this state too, so skipping only
# defers it.
salt wgq.wg-icons
# The dom0 entrypoint: symlinks /usr/local/bin/wgq into the reviewed
# tree, so `sudo wgq zone add <zone>` works instead of the /srv/salt
# path, and `wgq provision ...` frames the qvm-run into wgq-mgmt.
salt wgq.wg-cli
# The wgq label namespace stays dom0's alone: explicit qrexec denies
# for admin.label.Create/Remove on wgq's own label names, so a later
# broad admin grant to some management qube can never rewrite them.
policy 30-wgq-labels.policy
# Only dom0 makes and dresses qubes: restates the Admin API's deny
# default for qube creation, cloning and label changes, so it survives
# any later broad allow. Removable if a management qube must someday
# create qubes -- but that day should be a decision, not an accident.
policy 30-wgq-creation.policy
# Create wgq-mgmt, the provisioning qube. Zones are NOT created here:
# they are user lifecycle, one deliberate command each --
#     sudo wgq zone add <zone>
salt wgq.wg-mgmt
# OPTIONAL -- answer 's' to skip: the qrexec grant that lets 'wgq firewall'
# apply the endpoint allowlist through a dom0 'ask' prompt. Without it, the
# tool prints a qvm-firewall block to paste instead.
policy 30-wgq.policy
